#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166750 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166588 :question/id #uuid "e535fe44-a3cb-5c11-831c-118b90582c0d" :question/math-academy-id "e-8259" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z) = e^{xy + z},$ where $x = s + t,$ $y = s-t$ and $z = -s^2.$ Calculate $\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/b5/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t), y = y(s,t)$ and $z = z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial t} = \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial x}{\\partial t} + \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial y}{\\partial t} + \\dfrac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial t}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x, y$ and $z\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y{e}^{xy+z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x{e}^{xy+z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={e}^{xy+z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =(s-t){e}^{(s+t)(s-t)-{s}^{2}}=(s-t){e}^{-{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(s+t){e}^{(s+t)(s-t)-{s}^{2}}=(s+t){e}^{-{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & ={e}^{(s+t)(s-t)-{s}^{2}}={e}^{-{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =(s-t){e}^{-{t}^{2}}\\cdot 1+(s+t){e}^{-{t}^{2}}\\cdot (-1)+{e}^{-{t}^{2}}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =(s-t-s-t){e}^{-{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =-2t{e}^{-{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "71c243ca-5d46-58d2-bd16-28075c04d2db" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97f1076d-2275-516b-961c-22d007abc51d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165178} {:answer/id #uuid "9f90df6b-00df-5525-9798-9ecd2bb5bec4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165179} {:answer/id #uuid "b6cba1c9-110e-52be-aefb-8c3b0399f4ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165180} {:answer/id #uuid "dc15f6c9-3a22-5445-942f-f22d2c447420" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165181} {:answer/id #uuid "75148fb9-9798-551b-aed5-10ca0ebad3a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165182}] :answer-field/id #uuid "108e0a08-2c63-58bb-8d35-52cf4cb72bb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165177} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a08b852d-dd88-5d77-8ddb-331167273436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378033} {:answer/id #uuid "f90bb410-5dcb-5f1b-9fb7-2aab135e836b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378034} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd0123d-db34-56ee-8e11-8923b0a7b1a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378035} {:answer/id #uuid "fe429b03-fa1d-52c0-9976-c7f30c69dfc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378036} {:answer/id #uuid "fbbc9cd2-e31f-514b-9f87-beb31da0389e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378037}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a08b852d-dd88-5d77-8ddb-331167273436" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378033} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e3b0fb6-3358-5fd4-9918-187307cf0084" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378032}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8b576dec-df7c-5124-81b5-502e3d89f6ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-94589" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+2xy-3{z}^{2},$ where $x=st,$ $y=s+3t,$ and $z=2s-t.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=2({s}^{2}t+{s}^{2}+{c}_{1}st+{c}_{2}s+{c}_{3}t),\n$$\n\nfind the value of ${c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/b5/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂t}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x+2y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-6z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2(st)+2(s+3t)=2st+2s+6t \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2st \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =-6(2s-t)=6t-12s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =s \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =3 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =(2st+2s+6t)\\cdot s+(2st)\\cdot 3+(6t-12s)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2{s}^{2}t+2{s}^{2}+6st+6st-6t+12s \\\\  & =2{s}^{2}t+2{s}^{2}+12st+12s-6t \\\\  & =2({s}^{2}t+{s}^{2}+6st+6s-3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${c}_{1}={c}_{2}=6,{c}_{3}=-3,$ and therefore\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}=6+6-3=9.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167329 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e066783-cc18-5eb2-9d21-8cb3a4a748c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-8s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358990} {:answer/id #uuid "a57c4441-187c-592c-9f74-30558617760e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t+4s-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359188} {:answer/id #uuid "c652e165-04e8-5bd4-b5ee-5437d0c90d76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359495} {:answer/id #uuid "ccfbe840-ca43-5ae5-9a3e-063511d91a96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t-3s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359553} {:answer/id #uuid "ea70d6ac-8610-5e44-8201-c1c2f2d2c708" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea70d6ac-8610-5e44-8201-c1c2f2d2c708" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359836} :answer-field/id #uuid "d669b597-8865-5ea9-b4c0-cfa956eb17ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360366}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db13dec0-b66e-50d3-9ee6-bdc2288dd174" :question/math-academy-id "q-94814" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=4x+3y-2z,$ where $x=2{s}^{2}-t,$ $y=s+3{t}^{2}$ and $z=4{s}^{2}+{t}^{2}.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=4,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=3,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =4s, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =8s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(4)\\cdot 4s+(3)\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 8s \\\\  & =16s+3-16s \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284670 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0846d8ac-217c-5fd0-9480-a245a8fb32df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281757} {:answer/id #uuid "3390d758-2eee-59f2-b281-5202d0af878a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282151} {:answer/id #uuid "ca69f0e4-75f3-50e2-9045-04b99ce39acf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283458} {:answer/id #uuid "cf9a9896-fab1-5267-a73b-efbd2002049c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283500} {:answer/id #uuid "ec3a6c74-8de8-5dd3-a5c7-a7d063aa2bb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3390d758-2eee-59f2-b281-5202d0af878a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282151} :answer-field/id #uuid "f863b767-90fc-5d51-a406-d14dbceafe99" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284375}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5342e0ff-5836-5e24-9c29-40f19b250df2" :question/math-academy-id "q-170675" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{y+z}{x},$ where $x=s+t,$ $y={s}^{2}$ and $z={t}^{2}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{{c}_{1}{s}^{2}+{c}_{2}st+{c}_{3}{t}^{2}}{(s+t)^{2}},\n$$\n\nfind the value of ${c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/b5/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\frac{y+z}{{x}^{2}},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-\\frac{{s}^{2}+{t}^{2}}{(s+t)^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{s+t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{1}{s+t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =0, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & =2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =-\\frac{{s}^{2}+{t}^{2}}{(s+t)^{2}}\\cdot (1)+\\frac{1}{s+t}\\cdot 0+\\frac{1}{s+t}\\cdot 2t \\\\  & =\\frac{-({s}^{2}+{t}^{2})+2t(s+t)}{(s+t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}+2ts-{s}^{2}}{(s+t)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${c}_{1}=-1,$ ${c}_{2}=2$ and ${c}_{3}=1,$ and therefore\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}=-1+2+1=2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323885 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a9a8991-24fd-50f9-8941-a329e3133c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{s}^{4}{t}^{2}+10{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321230} {:answer/id #uuid "84b790fb-dce2-5ea5-9fbd-fb66967b78c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{s}^{2}{t}^{4}-20s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322195} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1f027a-f67b-5d1f-b407-9ee3b85b3667" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{s}^{4}t-5{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322598} {:answer/id #uuid "c8bfc905-fde6-54a5-83ad-c5fa1e325d7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{s}^{4}{t}^{2}-20{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322709} {:answer/id #uuid "f675ee7a-8c5d-5a9a-90cb-d0e4dd971fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{s}^{2}{t}^{4}-15s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8bfc905-fde6-54a5-83ad-c5fa1e325d7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{s}^{4}{t}^{2}-20{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322709} :answer-field/id #uuid "af1de9ae-38d9-5d66-a275-9fc76c319cbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323509}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bd5b5db6-0961-5b1c-8f50-24c2f4348bc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-37132" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}y-5yz,$ where $x=st,$ $y={s}^{3}$ and $z=s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2xy,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={x}^{2}-5z,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=-5y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2(st)({s}^{3})=2{s}^{4}t, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =(st)^{2}-5(s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)={s}^{2}{t}^{2}-5s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =-5{s}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =t, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =3{s}^{2}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(2{s}^{4}t)\\cdot t+({s}^{2}{t}^{2}-5s\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 3{s}^{2}+(-5{s}^{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =2{s}^{4}{t}^{2}+3{s}^{4}{t}^{2}-15{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-5{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\  & =5{s}^{4}{t}^{2}-20{s}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08fc4780-527f-5686-a54d-abb89b220c36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357832} {:answer/id #uuid "b6b12e0c-b95b-5473-906d-837cd6ca25f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5t+4s-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359338} {:answer/id #uuid "d526a50b-7e3f-5fc3-bb9e-6e2833f01728" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8t-s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359615} {:answer/id #uuid "eaa5887a-199b-5b40-8eff-86703cb3bfe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359841} {:answer/id #uuid "ebfb289f-dfba-5fc0-a653-13f7660f68c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t-s-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359852}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08fc4780-527f-5686-a54d-abb89b220c36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357832} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc4f8771-2072-5512-a9d1-948309d3d440" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360345}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4381d9a9-c913-5a57-ad60-d264f0f8dbf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-94811" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=3x-2y+z,$ where $x=s+t,$ $y={s}^{2}-{t}^{2}$ and $z=s.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/b5/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂t}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=3,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-2,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =-2t, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =(3)\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-2t)+(1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =4t+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10e508df-6b3b-5619-bd00-1b8b8babca29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s(t+1){e}^{t+s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357893} {:answer/id #uuid "5d52108c-0835-5be2-9ed4-59a5991f49cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t(s+1){e}^{t+s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358564} {:answer/id #uuid "98d94341-06cf-5f4b-bc8d-93a6314fa31b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(t+s){e}^{t+s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359092} {:answer/id #uuid "b829b030-9374-5df6-a2a6-5ccca1a395a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4t(s-1){e}^{t+s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359349} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf13666-86a4-5895-a4b1-0d044e43b4c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(t-s){e}^{t+s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10e508df-6b3b-5619-bd00-1b8b8babca29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2s(t+1){e}^{t+s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357893} :answer-field/id #uuid "eadd02ce-4767-57e9-98d3-5dceb4d1327c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360416}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8b931e70-9d8d-58d8-83d5-a3ea5f463c4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-94812" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=xyz,$ where $x=2,$ $y=s{e}^{t}$ and $z=t{e}^{s}.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/b5/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=yz,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=xz,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=xy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =ts{e}^{t+s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2t{e}^{s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =2s{e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =0, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =s{e}^{t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & ={e}^{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =(ts{e}^{t+s})\\cdot 0+(2t{e}^{s})\\cdot s{e}^{t}+(2s{e}^{t})\\cdot {e}^{s} \\\\  & =2ts{e}^{t+s}+2s{e}^{t+s} \\\\  & =2s(t+1){e}^{t+s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0047f2c1-1694-5db5-a45f-e4e293a64ff1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({t}^{2}-1){e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357754} {:answer/id #uuid "1c595ea9-356e-59e5-bc0c-b335e1d8a5a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357995} {:answer/id #uuid "82b282db-0082-5da1-8d0f-a5cfca996888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(t+2){e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358900} {:answer/id #uuid "87828807-8452-5466-bb74-63b110cd234c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "st{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358938} {:answer/id #uuid "ac64ab70-2776-54f6-90ad-be4c6bd57630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{t}^{2}{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359235}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c595ea9-356e-59e5-bc0c-b335e1d8a5a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357995} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7cd8dcb-b0f6-5528-9d87-abea84c22070" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360337}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e0e34c19-8056-5c3e-8be3-3398dc28d15e" :question/math-academy-id "q-94813" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)={e}^{x+y+z},$ where $x=s-t,$ $y={t}^{2}$ and $z=s+t.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/b5/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}={e}^{x+y+z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}={e}^{x+y+z},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={e}^{x+y+z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & ={e}^{(s-t)+{t}^{2}+(s+t)}={e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={e}^{(s-t)+{t}^{2}+(s+t)}={e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & ={e}^{(s-t)+{t}^{2}+(s+t)}={e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =2t, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =({e}^{2s+{t}^{2}})\\cdot (-1)+({e}^{2s+{t}^{2}})\\cdot 2t+({e}^{2s+{t}^{2}})\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}+2t{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}+{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =2t{e}^{2s+{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360510 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c63ba2d-fffd-5ea7-ac15-33befec87a20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s(t+s)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358827} {:answer/id #uuid "999f2f54-67a3-50e6-b7d4-c629f08c9bad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t(5-s)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359100} {:answer/id #uuid "c7cc85c1-989f-5e4b-99f2-dde3a379fedd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(st+s-t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359509} {:answer/id #uuid "dcc0bc08-7a90-588c-9d33-3108cf46a58f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(5s-t+s{t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359690} {:answer/id #uuid "ec51930c-d788-57bf-9004-06129c3fa9b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3s-5t-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcc0bc08-7a90-588c-9d33-3108cf46a58f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(5s-t+s{t}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359690} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc844387-da57-56cb-b663-9a5de9135b9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360446}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e1a4443a-d602-5476-a3eb-e3b0f2ea7373" :question/math-academy-id "q-94815" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2},$ where $x=t+2s,$ $y=3t-s$ and $z=st.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2(t+2s)=2t+4s, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2(3t-s)=6t-2s, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =2st.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =2, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =-1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(2t+4s)\\cdot 2+(6t-2s)\\cdot (-1)+(2st)\\cdot t \\\\  & =4t+8s-6t+2s+2s{t}^{2} \\\\  & =10s-2t+2s{t}^{2} \\\\  & =2(5s-t+s{t}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360511 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a5af5ec-c0b6-5eb3-b176-445a0d64ec5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{st+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357840} {:answer/id #uuid "37420b87-3117-59f2-b728-c9c475c83bd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+{t}^{2}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358239} {:answer/id #uuid "6d72e3f6-f856-5a2d-8aa4-ab886f7050c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{t}^{2}-{s}^{2}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358707} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d11231-84ab-5f98-8698-5dae52d58fd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "st({s}^{2}{t}^{2}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359190} {:answer/id #uuid "ca9fee15-8119-5226-90c5-c0c8229a0955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(1+2{s}^{2})}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca9fee15-8119-5226-90c5-c0c8229a0955" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(1+2{s}^{2})}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359527} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbd7eed6-1774-5bc4-bcdf-de25640be411" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360344}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e95a8899-bb64-5745-b230-495ea8deeef9" :question/math-academy-id "q-94816" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2{e}^{y}+4z,$ where $x=t{s}^{2},$ $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+{s}^{2})$ and $z={s}^{2}.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=\\frac{1}{x},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-2{e}^{y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{t{s}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =-2{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}+{s}^{2})}=-2({t}^{2}+{s}^{2}), \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =2ts, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =\\frac{2s}{{t}^{2}+{s}^{2}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(\\frac{1}{t{s}^{2}})\\cdot 2ts+(-2({t}^{2}+{s}^{2}))\\cdot (\\frac{2s}{{t}^{2}+{s}^{2}})+(4)\\cdot 2s \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-4s+8s \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}+4s \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1+2{s}^{2})}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383614 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8172957c-8ded-58d3-9a23-800391f6abc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383616} {:answer/id #uuid "65fc28e8-01f1-5779-81a2-95006d854621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{s}-2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383617} {:answer/id #uuid "78f76e21-a29b-5ac4-bef0-5e96cc36b301" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{s}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383618} {:answer/id #uuid "1650585c-4f5b-5c09-98dc-1b8f36155d98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{s}+2+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383619} {:answer/id #uuid "9d243851-27bb-5ff4-9d66-8de5b61c5110" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{s}+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383620}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78f76e21-a29b-5ac4-bef0-5e96cc36b301" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{s}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383618} :answer-field/id #uuid "a31244f4-c1a2-50a4-adcb-bc5510fae670" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383615}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04777d40-e9e1-5da3-94ee-34ffd4874f77" :question/math-academy-id "q-170674" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=z-x-y,$ where $x={e}^{s}+t,$ $y=s+1$ and $z=1-t-s.$ Calculate $\\frac{∂f}{∂s}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-1,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & ={e}^{s}, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(-1)\\cdot {e}^{s}+(-1)\\cdot 1+(1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-{e}^{s}-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "894ca471-2dd4-5d40-b36a-8da27b160d4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385372} {:answer/id #uuid "a0652b0f-d1a7-5fb6-a24a-41d904eaf606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385373} {:answer/id #uuid "290a2a7e-ad92-516f-ae90-67ba3132c946" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385374} {:answer/id #uuid "5ad83d4e-e307-5e90-9e4f-cc60c72f71d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385375} {:answer/id #uuid "10e3eea0-e64b-5459-8cc2-03bcb5ecde36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ad83d4e-e307-5e90-9e4f-cc60c72f71d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385375} :answer-field/id #uuid "98ca2715-a0aa-5460-b75b-4a47465638ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385371}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7b9407c6-12a8-5179-a6fb-edc61bbc79bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-37208" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+{y}^{2}z,$ where $x=3t,$ $y=t-s$ and $z=2st.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+{c}_{1}s{t}^{2}+{c}_{2}{s}^{2}t+{c}_{3}{s}^{3},\n$$\n\nfind the value of ${c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/b5/b593a1b60fe8c1aef2c5c229ff426db350e6296b9ecb767494283f0fa3342072.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=2yz,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}={y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =2(t-s)(2st)=4s{t}^{2}-4{s}^{2}t, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =(t-s)^{2}={t}^{2}-2st+{s}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂t} & =3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂t} & =1, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂t} & =2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂t} & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)\\cdot 3+(4s{t}^{2}-4{s}^{2}t)\\cdot 1+({t}^{2}-2st+{s}^{2})\\cdot 2s \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+4s{t}^{2}-4{s}^{2}t+2s{t}^{2}-4{s}^{2}t+2{s}^{3} \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t+6s{t}^{2}-8{s}^{2}t+2{s}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${c}_{1}=6,$ ${c}_{2}=-8$ and ${c}_{3}=2,$ and therefore\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}=6+(-8)+2=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420996 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17573a89-2ada-5cfd-8592-1b89b18d61f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420990} {:answer/id #uuid "3856cad9-d2c1-55a4-adf6-784ae35a6aa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420991} {:answer/id #uuid "5c54b913-d15a-53bc-b2c6-f71477530f9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420992} {:answer/id #uuid "ae277bb1-236f-56f1-8a0c-7fd47295108c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420993} {:answer/id #uuid "d87585d5-b5cd-5fbc-b58c-a3d2c45f4e66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae277bb1-236f-56f1-8a0c-7fd47295108c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420993} :answer-field/id #uuid "f118ee24-10a3-5bda-8238-4be0365cace0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420995}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f22c7a35-af74-59c8-b71b-cae8347ea97d" :question/math-academy-id "q-37206" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=xy+yz+{z}^{2},$ where $x={s}^{2}+{t}^{2},$ $y=\\frac{s}{t}$ and $z=s{t}^{2}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{3{s}^{2}}{t}+{c}_{1}t+{c}_{2}st+{c}_{3}s{t}^{4},\n$$\n\nfind the value of ${c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x+z,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=y+2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{s}{t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={s}^{2}+{t}^{2}+s{t}^{2}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{s}{t}+2s{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =2s, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =\\frac{1}{t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & ={t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(\\frac{s}{t})\\cdot 2s+({s}^{2}+{t}^{2}+s{t}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+(\\frac{s}{t}+2s{t}^{2})\\cdot {t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}}{t}+\\frac{{s}^{2}}{t}+t+st+st+2s{t}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{s}^{2}}{t}+t+2st+2s{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${c}_{1}=1,$ ${c}_{2}=2$ and ${c}_{3}=2,$ and therefore\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}=1+2+2=5.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Derivative of a Function of Three Intermediate Variables and Two Independent Variables"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166813 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166651 :question/id #uuid "cafdc3de-f065-5a60-be3e-8521a49929d4" :question/math-academy-id "e-8459" :question/problem "What is the order of the ordinary differential equation $2x\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}^3y}{\\textrm{d}x^3}+y^2\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}^2y}{\\textrm{d}x^2}=3x^2?$" :question/worked-solution "The order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}^3y}{\\textrm{d}x^3},$ which has order $3.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $3.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "443c0bd0-2e77-50a8-91d3-a288d4ee852b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167439 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f4efdc2-0db6-5c05-93a3-dc37ed677c69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358025} {:answer/id #uuid "259dd133-5bb9-5064-ab22-10c2ff0d0e41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358091} {:answer/id #uuid "51e56ff6-776f-5f56-9c5b-1b8c442dae31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358457} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e79109-ddec-555e-b8e9-91c639217e9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359730} {:answer/id #uuid "e1b99836-5aa4-5130-9573-30541e38e184" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51e56ff6-776f-5f56-9c5b-1b8c442dae31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358457} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0ef61cf-9080-52a8-9361-8ad5a39a4f1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360394}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b6d57756-51a0-53da-bab4-6debeaf1e4ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-95982" :question/problem "What is the order of the ordinary differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{x}^{3}y=5{y}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}},$ which has order $2.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167440 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68bd231d-9e13-571c-877b-269bf3710fa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422255} {:answer/id #uuid "7ed54d05-d26e-52c1-9f98-8a77b88ca5f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ed54d05-d26e-52c1-9f98-8a77b88ca5f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422256} :answer-field/id #uuid "f322ec74-487b-53f0-b9c7-a8290b3eeda9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422408} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "690c87af-9ba3-5188-a6c9-7004cd7ed245" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422257} {:answer/id #uuid "3abb4d56-10ee-58da-b334-bd3d4d312f6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "690c87af-9ba3-5188-a6c9-7004cd7ed245" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422257} :answer-field/id #uuid "97cd6e48-b23a-590e-a423-5f82ee6788fa" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 1759