ential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234491 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d0d894d-c809-5dae-b04c-777fa7f1b329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422291} {:answer/id #uuid "3ef08266-c8b5-5d86-ba6c-38cec94b0b81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422292}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d0d894d-c809-5dae-b04c-777fa7f1b329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422291} :answer-field/id #uuid "34bc34b4-9e03-56ed-af57-5921ddebb2d3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422426} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccb30e5b-1e6e-5289-8a92-1d1a6eb3264f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422293} {:answer/id #uuid "5090af3c-f638-5321-a137-c61895760b06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccb30e5b-1e6e-5289-8a92-1d1a6eb3264f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422293} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b81d3a8-27c9-5a56-9c75-a52909222499" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422427} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7601c375-892a-5f42-948b-dc68c11393c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422295} {:answer/id #uuid "4fae8008-076c-53ed-87cb-e76c044c94bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fae8008-076c-53ed-87cb-e76c044c94bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422296} :answer-field/id #uuid "a78a9497-be8a-530e-9cb5-154e8f8d6f0c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422428}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "85cea071-187a-5be3-b347-b4aa26aead57" :question/math-academy-id "q-96680" :question/problem "Which of the following are first-order ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $3{y}^{'}+2x{y}^{''}={x}^{2}y$\n- **II.** $5{x}^{2}{y}^{‴}+3x{y}^{'}={e}^{x}$\n- **III.** $4{({y}^{'})}^{3}+7{x}^{3}=x({y}^{2}+{({y}^{'})}^{2})$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of first-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation I is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{''},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation II is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation III is a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ecd7d48-e192-56ba-a9eb-6c4280135677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ecd7d48-e192-56ba-a9eb-6c4280135677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234667} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1bfa42a-8d4e-593c-aa9b-c50e784fddb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235263}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "615b21ea-17f4-5ce5-8433-316c3df76ca0" :question/math-academy-id "q-167787" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{4}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{4}}-x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x)\n$$\n\nThe order of this differential equation is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "We have the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{4}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{4}}-x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{4}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{4}},$ which has order $4.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22ac80f9-d1a9-57b5-8a75-ee4e690886f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250849} {:answer/id #uuid "254a46ec-eea5-5a9e-b90d-ccb407bc95b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250874} {:answer/id #uuid "625479f9-bef7-5c1a-937a-158ca732f7fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251352} {:answer/id #uuid "c2b7f046-3e73-5ab4-abac-a3903f00d5ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252273} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ca56e0-ad02-5c3f-97f9-85ad61671b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/